WEBVTT

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.440
[Uhtred] I was born

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.440
an Aelderman of England.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.840
Uhtred, son of Uhtred

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.840
of Bebbanburg,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.640
welcome to the Christian world.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.680
[Uhtred] True heir to the

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.680
Northumbrian lands of Bebbanburg.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:16.920
You have your stone,

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:16.920
the amber?

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.520
Yes, Father.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.440
Our ancestors took this land and

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.440
you will die for it, if needed.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.720
<i> I was 12-years-old</i>

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.720
<i> when I first went to war.</i>

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.080
[man] Kill them all!

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.920
<i> I saw my father killed.</i>

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.800
<i> My Uncle took my lands</i>

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.360
<i> and pledged his allegiance</i>

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.360
<i> to the Danes.</i>

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.720
My advice to you

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.720
is never to cross Ubba

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.440
<i> and never, never fight him.</i>

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.040
[Uhtred]

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.040
Stolen by the invaders,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.320
along with

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.320
the Saxon girl, Brida.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.320
I became first a slave,

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.320
and then a son to Earl Ragnar.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.840
That was my family. My life.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.320
Young Ragnar, my brother,

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.320
and Brida, my lover.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.520
Fate had made me a Dane.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.840
And then fate brought betrayal.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.520
[yelling]

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.400
I will not stand by and have

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.400
everything that's mine taken from me.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.280
Bebbanburg's is mine!

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.120
<i> Destiny is all.</i>

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.160
Horses!

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.960
Head for the woods.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.240
[yelling indistinct]

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.080
Go right, there's a gully

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.080
over that ridge.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.840
Hoof-marks.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.840
There must be hoof-marks.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.920
There must be hoof-marks

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.920
somewhere!

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.360
Fetch more men.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.360
I want him found!

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.320
We'll go as far as Mercia

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.320
if need be,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.400
but I want him found

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.400
and I want him dead.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.080
He looked like my father.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.200
And now he knows you are alive,

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.200
he'll keep looking for you.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.640
Let him. I'm going to kill him

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.640
and take back what's mine.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.920
He has an army.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.920
He is the choice of the Danes!

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.080
All you have is me!

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.200
No, we have Ubba.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.040
We go to him with our story.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.680
With his army, we avenge Ragnar's

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.680
death and we take back Bebbanburg.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.400
It's that simple?

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.200
Yes.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.880
Yes...

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.080
[Uhtred]<i> </i>Brida...

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.560
Brida... sing me a song.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.000
I won't,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.000
and I'm not your skald.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.520
True, and what's more,

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.520
you'd frighten the birds.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:05.960
What?

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.480
There is a taste in the air.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.480
Death.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.720
[birds chirping]

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.760
[arrow hisses]

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.880
[panting]

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.680
[arrow hisses]

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.080
[grunts]

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.440
Who did this?

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.440
Who sacked the village?

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:52.800
[man] I cannot move.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:54.240
Your back is broken.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.520
[groans in pain]

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.120
Who did it?

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.480
You know who did this.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.480
Danes did this.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.080
Why?

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.760
I don't believe you,

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.560
why should the Danes attack

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.560
a village that feeds them?

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.480
Revenge.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.240
But since when have

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.240
Danes needed an excuse to kill?

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.280
[Brida]

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.280
Revenge, revenge for what?

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.800
Huh?

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.200
Revenge for what,

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.200
and I'll end it.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:23.720
An uprising north of here.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:28.160
A Saxon slave, he killed

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:28.160
his master at a wedding party.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:32.320
[man gasping]

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.480
What was the name of the slave?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.320
Huh?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.720
You speak English well

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.720
for a Dane.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.160
His name!

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.120
[groans]

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.080
Uhtred.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.320
End it.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.440
End...

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.520
[groans in pain]

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.360
-Say it...

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.360
-Say what?

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:11.800
What you are thinking.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.200
I'm thinking

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.200
that you have a turd

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.400
where there's

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.400
supposed to be a mind?

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.680
[laughing]

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.680
Thank you.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.880
We should never

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.880
have gone to Bebbanburg.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.800
We should have let them

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.800
believe that you were dead!

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:31.120
No, you're wrong.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:31.120
I want them to know I am alive.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.320
I need them to know I am alive

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.320
because they hold what's mine.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.280
I feel better for it.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.120
Yeah, so does a dog

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.120
pissing on a tree.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.480
You wish me to bark?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.520
What we needed to do was to ride

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.520
south to the Chieftain Ubba,

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.040
and tell the story

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.040
of Ragnar's death.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.520
We'll do it now.

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.120
Now there is a second story,

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.320
about some slave

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.320
who killed his master.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.960
Ubba knows that Ragnar

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.960
was my father.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:00.520
He knows nothing!

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:00.520
I doubt he'll even remember you!

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.320
He will believe the story

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.320
that he hears first!

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.040
And he will kill you.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.080
If you could write,

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.080
then you could write to him.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.560
If he could read.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.040
You've left us no choice.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.160
We must find Ubba

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.160
and hope he believes you.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:37.840
[indistinct chatter]

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:37.840
[bell tolling]

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.600
Thank you.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:57.680
[man] Father Beocca.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.600
Father.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.160
Segwall.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.440
I'll see you in the King's Hall.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:25.360
My Lord?

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:30.800
My Lord Alfred,

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:30.800
it is I, Father Beocca.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:34.040
My Lord,

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:34.040
the king has called council.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.360
[Alfred]

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.360
Do not look at me Father.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:40.160
I am a sinner

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:40.160
I'm a grievous sinner.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.920
We are all sinners, my Lord.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.800
And I am married!

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.800
I should never have married.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.600
He sends temptation to test us.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:50.520
And when we fail he sends the Danes

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:50.520
to punish us for that failure.

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.560
[Alfred] I should never have married,

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.560
I should have joined the church

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.640
I should of gone to a monastery.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.720
And God would have found

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.720
a great servant in you,

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.440
but I feel he has other plans.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:03.600
If your brother were to die, it would

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:03.600
be to you, the people would turn.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.440
Oh, pray God he does not die.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:09.280
What kind of king would I be?

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:12.080
You'll be God's king,

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:12.080
my Lord.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.360
You have been blessed and chosen

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.360
by the Holy Father in Rome,

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.720
you would be God's king.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.800
I have seen the girl who

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.800
torments you. She is...

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.160
-She must be banished.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.160
-No, I believe the opposite.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.600
She should be

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.600
brought into your service.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.680
-No, no I could not.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.680
-You will resist her.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.880
You will let Him

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.880
see your strength.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.080
You will thank Him

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.080
for tempting you

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.400
and then praise Him

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.400
for resisting the temptation.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.600
Notwithstanding...

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.760
I have news

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.760
you may wish to take to council.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.040
What news?

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.080
Of an English uprising,

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.080
Lord, in the north.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.840
It was defeated.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:57.480
But the nobleman responsible was

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:57.480
Uhtred of Bebbanburg, I know him.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:02.200
He was taken by the Danes

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:02.200
as a child, a God-fearing child.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:04.120
Clearly his heart

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:04.120
remains English.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:07.560
-He lives?

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:07.560
-I believe so.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.880
He is a warrior, Lord.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:11.760
They say he killed his

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:11.760
Danish master and 40 men.

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:13.720
He knows their ways,

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:13.720
he speaks their language.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:14.880
He would be useful,

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:14.880
would he not?

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.120
You could mention him

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.120
in council?

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:18.960
Why would

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:18.960
he kill his master?

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.880
For blood?

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.880
For money? For pleasure?

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:23.800
-For England, Lord.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:23.800
-Yes, but how do we know?

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:28.120
He may well be just one more

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:28.120
Pagan with a busy sword.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.360
Ah, but I know him Lord.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:32.040
No, Father Beocca,

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:32.040
you knew him, once.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.880
You knew him as a child.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.600
I could send word out

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.600
into the country, God willing.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:39.320
Father, he's a ghost,

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:39.320
he's a Pagan rumor.

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:42.600
Should he become flesh and blood,

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:42.600
then he may merit a mention.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:47.480
However, my faith,

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:47.480
I reserve for God alone.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.840
Now about this girl?

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.840
You may be right about her.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:59.120
Bring her into my personal

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:59.120
service... and pray for me.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:01.960
As always, my Lord.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.120
[indistinct chatter]

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.960
Alfred.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.000
King Edmund of East Anglia writes

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.000
a plea to Wessex, for an army.

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:19.920
An attack by the Danish Chieftain,

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:19.920
Earl Ubba, is inevitable.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.400
This was two days ago.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.880
A long march to fight the Danes

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.880
at a place of their choosing

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:26.800
is not a strategy

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:26.800
worth considering.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:29.560
-To say the least, my Lord.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:29.560
-I am of a mind to decline.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:30.840
-And rightly.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:30.840
-Ubba...

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.840
...he is the Dane

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.840
whom King Edmund

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.680
-has fed and watered in the past?

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.680
-He is.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.920
Perhaps in the hope that he

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.920
would simply pass through

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.640
East Anglia on his way

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.640
to invading Wessex.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.080
It is my opinion that Edmond

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.080
deserves nothing but silence.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.680
Too harsh, young Odda.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.680
I believe it was Edmund's hope

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.800
to convert the Danes

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.800
from Pagan to Christian,

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:50.000
beginning with charity.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.440
For that

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.440
he deserves praise, surely.

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.640
You are true, my Lord,

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.640
if indeed that was his hope.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:58.560
Edmund is a Godly man, we have no reason

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:58.560
to mistake his actions for cowardice.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:01.120
[Aethelred] Regardless of Edmund's

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:01.120
intentions barring a miracle,

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.200
East Anglia will soon

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.200
fall to the Danes.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.720
And he shall have all our prayers

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.720
for such a miracle, my Lord.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.040
He will need them.

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.200
He will not, however,

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.200
have one man of Wessex,

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.120
-on that we are agreed?

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.120
-Yes, Lord.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.360
[all agreeing]

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.480
Then we must therefore recognize

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.480
that we now stand alone.

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.640
The last kingdom of England.

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:23.400
It will soon be the men of Wessex staring

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:23.400
across a field at the Pagan Army.

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:26.600
We must be ready. We must

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:26.600
pray and we must prepare.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:31.000
Odda, I require Mercia, Lundene and

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:31.000
East Anglia to be watched carefully.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.160
Forward knowledge is everything.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.920
-It is done, my Lord.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.920
-And, scribe,

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.560
I require the forges

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.560
of every town and village

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:36.920
to be burning, night and day.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.280
We shall need all the iron

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.280
those fires can proffer.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.360
Yes, my Lord.

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:44.400
Most of all I require men.

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:47.120
Strong, fighting men

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.560
who are prepared to die

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.560
because that in the end,

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.640
is what it will

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.640
take to save us...

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.920
...the blood of men.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:03.720
Ravn used to say,

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:03.720
"Never fight Ubba."

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:09.400
Looks like East Anglia's

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:09.400
just made that mistake.

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:14.720
We should stay away for now.

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:16.960
Build our own fire.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.200
Ubba's unpredictable,

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:22.480
he takes his orders

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:22.480
from the Gods.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.880
[Uhtred] I know,

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.880
he only listens to a sorcerer.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.280
And he's half mad.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.600
How will you approach him?

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:31.240
As a man.

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:35.640
It has to be done.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:41.120
Yes, it has to be done.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:41.120
But we need to guard your life.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:44.680
-How?

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:44.680
-I don't know.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.600
We should hump, tonight.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:58.400
We should, it's written.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.760
That we should hump?

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:06.040
[chuckles] Our destiny is to hump...

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:06.040
tonight.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:08.360
[chuckles]

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:21.520
I'm enjoying the thought of it.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.400
That's all

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.400
you'll enjoy tonight.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.520
[chuckles]

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.960
[moaning]

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:35.040
-Stop, stop, stop!

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:35.040
-What? What is it?

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.480
I... I think I have it.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:44.240
We take a hostage, a shield

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:44.240
a guarantee for your life.

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.200
Who?

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:50.960
I don't know...

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:50.960
someone he can't do without.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:55.000
Storri. His sorcerer.

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:57.920
[screaming]

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:10.600
[man]

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:10.600
Who is the woman?

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.280
Why is she not on her back?

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:16.080
Not that it's your concern,

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:16.080
but she's for Storri,

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.200
a Saxon whore from Ubba.

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:19.800
I've seen you before.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:23.520
I served Earl Ragnar,

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:23.520
and now I serve Ubba.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:25.000
[woman screaming]

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.760
You'll see me again,

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.760
I'm sure, boy.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.600
[chuckles]

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:31.400
I'm told Storri

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:31.400
is at the church.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:32.920
He's up at the Monastery,

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.920
looking after King Edmond

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.920
and killing his priests.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.480
[coughing]

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.120
[man groans]

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.760
Hello?

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:09.160
Leave me or it will be

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:09.160
the death of you!

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:11.760
The church is mine,

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:11.760
by the order of Ubba.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.800
Master Storri,

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.800
I have a gift for you.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:16.000
-Really?

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:16.000
-She is from Earl Ubba.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:19.400
A woman?

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:19.400
Why would Ubba send me a woman?

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:21.800
-I have no need of a woman.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:21.800
-She is a sorceress.

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:24.480
He wishes her dead

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:24.480
but is afraid of a curse.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:29.040
Saggy tits, stinking breath,

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:29.040
but you will be rewarded.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:31.120
Her head's weight in silver.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.400
A sorceress?

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:37.720
She has the face of a she-wolf.

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:37.720
Does she bite?

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:41.760
-Yes, she bites.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:41.760
-Leave her with me.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:45.160
I will do as Ubba asks,

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:45.160
and she will die... slowly.

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:47.000
[grunts]

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:50.440
You belong to me now, old man.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:54.280
And you will die slowly

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:54.280
unless you do as I say.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.560
On your feet,

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.560
we're going for a walk,

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.560
and you will

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.560
keep your mouth shut!

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:05.800
This is so foolish,

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:09.360
Ubba will come look for me,

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:09.360
and he will be here soon.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.880
I said be quiet.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:14.680
Then I'll wait for him here.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:14.680
I'll wait for Ubba here.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:19.080
That means

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:19.080
it's just you and me.

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:30.920
[horse whinnies]

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:37.240
[man] Where is Storri,

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:37.240
he's supposed to be here?

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.840
Edmund?

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.200
Edmund...

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:47.160
Edmund...

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:50.560
Ed...

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:50.560
[laughing]

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:52.280
Can we have some ale?

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:55.040
Miserable King Edmund

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:55.040
of East Anglia,

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:58.400
you have had the night

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:58.400
to consider my offer.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:00.440
How do you answer?

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:02.000
[chuckles]

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:04.040
Are you dead

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:04.040
or breathing still?

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:07.800
With luck, he's dead. We allow far

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:07.800
too many of them to live as it is.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.240
-You allow nothing!

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.240
-He lives.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.280
It's God who decides who lives.

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.960
I would say your God

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.960
has left you hanging, sir.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:20.000
If he has done so,

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:20.000
it's because it is his will.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:23.120
Take him down,

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:23.120
and do not to let him fall,

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.480
and ale,

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.480
and for the Earl Guthrum.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.800
I don't understand,

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.800
we do that all time.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:29.160
We allow half of them to live.

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:31.920
I say we kill them all,

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:31.920
all but the young women.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.280
And who should work the fields?

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:36.320
The old women,

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:36.320
the pregnant women.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.800
Put him there,

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.800
and give the man some ale.

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:41.360
Earl Ubba!

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:44.480
If I may speak freely.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:48.080
-I know you.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:48.080
-I am Uhtred Ragnarson.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.120
I am here with the truth

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.120
of how my father died.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:54.320
Yes, you are Ragnar's slave,

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:54.320
and you killed him.

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:56.440
I don't know what stories

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:56.440
you've heard but Earl Ragnar

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.400
was killed by his own, by Danes.

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:02.160
His former ship's master, Kjartan

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:02.160
and his half-blind son, Sven,

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:04.280
they led the attack on a

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:04.280
sleeping wedding party.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.280
Can't you see that we are

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.280
entertaining a king?

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:09.000
Lord Ubba, I am telling you that

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:09.000
Earl Ragnar was killed by Danes!

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.440
You will be quiet boy!

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.440
And you will wait!

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.280
-Kill him.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.280
-Not another word!

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:15.960
Bar the doors,

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:15.960
he does not leave.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.600
Guthrum is right we are

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.600
entertaining a king,

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:20.440
so no more interruptions.

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:24.800
I just have to know,

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:24.800
who is that? Mmm!

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:29.720
-His eyes are watching me.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:29.720
-And me.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:32.440
Who's... Who's what? Who?

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:34.680
The half-naked image there...

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:37.600
Who is it?

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:38.800
[sighs]

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.440
That is the Saint Sebastian.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:42.920
A former Roman soldier

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:42.920
who found God.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.480
[Guthrum]

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.480
Found him where?

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:47.760
He... he found him in his heart!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:47.760
Not...

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:51.760
Do you wish me

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:51.760
to tell you his story?

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:53.760
I have time.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:02.120
The Emperor of Rome, on discovering

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:02.120
that Sebastian had found God,

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.760
ordered him to renounce

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.760
his faith, he refused.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:10.720
So then the Emperor ordered that he'd

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:10.720
be filled full of arrows and yet...

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:11.960
...he lived.

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:15.160
-He lived?

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:15.160
-Yes, he did.

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:17.440
-Is this true?

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:17.440
-Of course, it's true.

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:21.720
God saved Saint Sebastian and God

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:21.720
should be praised for that mercy.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.600
For how long did he live?

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:26.280
Well, sadly he...

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:29.480
He then ordered that

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:29.480
he be clubbed to death.

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:32.320
So he died.

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:35.360
He went to heaven,

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:35.360
so he lived.

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.280
I have heard

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.280
mention of this heaven.

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.040
What is this heaven?

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:40.200
Heaven is Valhalla, Lord.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:41.440
To the Christians,

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:41.440
but without

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:42.720
the fighting, feasting

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:42.720
and humping.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:47.360
Heaven is Heaven,

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:47.360
it is not heathen!

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:50.400
But to answer

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:50.400
your very first question,

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:53.320
I... I have considered

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:53.320
your offer and yes,

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:56.200
I will continue to rule

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:56.200
East Anglia as you suggest.

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:58.360
I will suffer your presence.

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:03.840
I will provide you with horses,

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:03.840
food, coin and hostages,

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:06.760
I will do all that you demand.

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:11.200
But... only if you,

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:17.520
Lord Ubba, and all

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:17.520
of your men... submit to God.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:22.400
That is my demand.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:22.400
You must be baptized.

00:22:25.400 --> 00:22:27.520
You must stand

00:22:25.400 --> 00:22:27.520
in a barrel of water,

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:30.360
and they pour

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:30.360
more water over you.

00:22:31.640 --> 00:22:33.320
They want to wash me?

00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:34.360
No...

00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:35.960
Your scent upsets them, Ubba.

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:37.880
No, to cleanse you

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:37.880
of your sin's,

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:41.040
there's only one God

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:41.040
and I demand that you serve him.

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:43.520
-Kill him now.

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:43.520
-Why must I serve him?

00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:46.240
Because God is great!

00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:46.240
All powerful! All magnificent!

00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:48.920
Have him stop

00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:48.920
his yapping and prove it!

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:52.280
Ah, agreed.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:52.280
Prove to me your god is great.

00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:55.760
-Prove it.

00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:55.760
-Prove, prove... look here.

00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:59.440
-God spared Saint Sebastian.

00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:59.440
-But the man still died.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:00.880
Because it was God's will!

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:02.680
So would your god

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:02.680
protect you from my arrows?

00:23:02.760 --> 00:23:04.480
If he was all powerful,

00:23:02.760 --> 00:23:04.480
he would.

00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:06.680
Yes, if it was God's will,

00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:06.680
he would, yes.

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.640
[Ubba]

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.640
So let us try.

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:13.640
We shall shoot arrows at you

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:13.640
and if you survive...

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:15.440
[chuckle]

00:23:15.520 --> 00:23:18.560
...we will all be washed.

00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:20.680
Including Guthrum here.

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:22.360
Why not?

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:30.480
Very well.

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:37.840
I will continue to be king,

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:40.760
but we will dispense

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:40.760
with the need for baptisms.

00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:42.920
The, uh... the washing.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:44.920
I withdraw my request.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:48.000
But you claim

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:48.000
your God is all powerful.

00:23:48.880 --> 00:23:50.800
I want it proven.

00:23:51.760 --> 00:23:53.560
Strip him.

00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:54.800
Archers.

00:24:00.760 --> 00:24:02.680
[Guthrum]

00:24:00.760 --> 00:24:02.680
Wait!

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:13.280
Tell me, truthfully,

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:13.280
are you afraid?

00:24:14.120 --> 00:24:16.280
God is great!

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:20.120
We will see.

00:24:25.160 --> 00:24:28.920
Shoot... Shoot!

00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:31.400
Ah...

00:24:31.480 --> 00:24:35.080
They are my men and only

00:24:31.480 --> 00:24:35.080
I tell them when to shoot.

00:24:36.920 --> 00:24:38.720
Shoot.

00:24:38.800 --> 00:24:40.920
[groaning]

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:44.000
[panting]

00:24:44.080 --> 00:24:48.080
Do you now wished to be clubbed,

00:24:44.080 --> 00:24:48.080
or will the arrows be sufficient?

00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:57.360
You have come a long way, boy, to tell me it

00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:57.360
was Danes, and not you, who killed Ragnar.

00:24:57.440 --> 00:25:02.520
It was Kjartan and Sven,

00:24:57.440 --> 00:25:02.520
Lord, and others.

00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:04.880
It's the truth.

00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:04.880
Why else would I be here?

00:25:04.960 --> 00:25:08.080
-To spy, to lie.

00:25:04.960 --> 00:25:08.080
-No, Lord.

00:25:08.160 --> 00:25:09.160
[laughing]

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:11.600
-Perhaps to kill me?

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:11.600
-No, Lord.

00:25:11.680 --> 00:25:13.960
Have you been washed?

00:25:14.840 --> 00:25:15.760
Odin is my God.

00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:18.120
But you have been washed?

00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:21.240
Yes, Lord.

00:25:21.320 --> 00:25:25.560
How did it feel... the washing?

00:25:25.640 --> 00:25:27.720
Cold, Lord.

00:25:25.640 --> 00:25:27.720
The water was cold.

00:25:27.800 --> 00:25:29.560
Nothing else?

00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:32.200
I was a child, Lord.

00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:32.200
Now I am a Dane.

00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:35.080
Yeah, a Dane.

00:25:40.240 --> 00:25:46.200
So now let us see if Odin will

00:25:40.240 --> 00:25:46.200
protect you from the arrows.

00:25:46.880 --> 00:25:49.000
I like this game. Strip him.

00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:51.680
-Keep away from me!

00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:51.680
-[grunting]

00:25:51.760 --> 00:25:53.840
-Not another step!

00:25:51.760 --> 00:25:53.840
-Archers at the ready!

00:25:53.920 --> 00:25:55.360
-I have a hostage!

00:25:53.920 --> 00:25:55.360
-What?

00:25:55.440 --> 00:25:57.000
-I have Storri!

00:25:55.440 --> 00:25:57.000
-Stop!

00:25:57.080 --> 00:25:58.320
If I die, he dies.

00:25:58.400 --> 00:26:00.120
If I die, your sorcerer dies

00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:01.240
and you're without his guidance.

00:26:01.320 --> 00:26:02.680
He lies, I can smell it.

00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:06.320
I have proof... his runes.

00:26:08.160 --> 00:26:10.480
Storri will be

00:26:08.160 --> 00:26:10.480
returned to you safely.

00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:12.400
Take his head

00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:12.400
from his shoulders!

00:26:12.480 --> 00:26:14.440
Guthrum, be quiet!

00:26:14.520 --> 00:26:16.040
Have them open the doors.

00:26:16.120 --> 00:26:19.600
I will release Storri

00:26:16.120 --> 00:26:19.600
when I am clear of this place.

00:26:19.680 --> 00:26:23.720
-You go nowhere! Then he dies!

00:26:19.680 --> 00:26:23.720
-Your sorcerer dies!

00:26:25.200 --> 00:26:27.760
Have them open the doors...

00:26:34.720 --> 00:26:36.920
[doors open]

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:42.400
One day I will kill you.

00:26:42.480 --> 00:26:46.680
Storri will tell you otherwise.

00:26:46.760 --> 00:26:50.320
And I am telling you the truth

00:26:46.760 --> 00:26:50.320
about Ragnar.

00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:03.720
This is what happens when we

00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:03.720
allow too many of them to live.

00:27:03.800 --> 00:27:05.840
[shouting]

00:27:07.360 --> 00:27:09.720
Excellent, firewood.

00:27:13.520 --> 00:27:15.720
You're alive.

00:27:15.800 --> 00:27:18.560
That's good.

00:27:15.800 --> 00:27:18.560
Did he hear you?

00:27:18.640 --> 00:27:23.280
-He did not. Not a word.

00:27:18.640 --> 00:27:23.280
-What did he say?

00:27:23.360 --> 00:27:26.240
-That he'll kill me.

00:27:23.360 --> 00:27:26.240
-Nothing else?

00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:28.160
Where's Storri?

00:27:28.880 --> 00:27:31.080
What did he say?

00:27:32.520 --> 00:27:35.440
-He's naked!

00:27:32.520 --> 00:27:35.440
-It was necessary.

00:27:35.520 --> 00:27:37.960
He has a branch

00:27:35.520 --> 00:27:37.960
up his arse.

00:27:38.040 --> 00:27:40.680
Which is why he is naked.

00:27:41.320 --> 00:27:42.840
Uhtred...

00:27:48.680 --> 00:27:49.920
[groans]

00:27:51.680 --> 00:27:56.080
Uhtred, he must have

00:27:51.680 --> 00:27:56.080
said something.

00:27:56.160 --> 00:27:57.960
He believes the lie.

00:27:58.040 --> 00:28:00.680
He believes that

00:27:58.040 --> 00:28:00.680
I killed Ragnar.

00:28:04.240 --> 00:28:09.080
[horse whinnies]

00:28:04.240 --> 00:28:09.080
[grunting]

00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:12.120
There's nothing more to do.

00:28:14.240 --> 00:28:16.480
[sighs]

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:19.160
We should put distance

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:19.160
between us and this place.

00:28:19.240 --> 00:28:20.480
And go where?

00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:23.280
Anywhere that's not here.

00:28:24.320 --> 00:28:26.840
I say we go to young Ragnar.

00:28:26.920 --> 00:28:29.400
-He's in Ireland.

00:28:26.920 --> 00:28:29.400
-Then we go to Ireland.

00:28:29.480 --> 00:28:33.160
How? In what? We sail in what?

00:28:29.480 --> 00:28:33.160
And with whom? Danes?

00:28:33.240 --> 00:28:34.840
Then we wait for him to return!

00:28:34.920 --> 00:28:37.320
What if he doesn't return,

00:28:34.920 --> 00:28:37.320
what then?

00:28:40.400 --> 00:28:42.880
Accept it, we're lost.

00:28:43.600 --> 00:28:45.360
We're alive

00:28:43.600 --> 00:28:45.360
and breathing for a reason.

00:28:45.440 --> 00:28:48.520
Brida, we are no longer Danes!

00:29:29.880 --> 00:29:32.200
How much for your work?

00:29:32.280 --> 00:29:34.120
For a long sword?

00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:36.720
You tell me what you need,

00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:36.720
and I'll tell you a price.

00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:39.760
A warrior sword

00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:39.760
to last a lifetime.

00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:45.000
And what are you?

00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:45.000
Saxon or Dane?

00:29:46.360 --> 00:29:47.840
Northumbria.

00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:52.880
It will take some time

00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:52.880
to make her right...

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.440
...which means

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.440
she'll be expensive.

00:29:56.520 --> 00:30:00.320
If she's right,

00:29:56.520 --> 00:30:00.320
I'll pay in silver. How much?

00:30:00.400 --> 00:30:02.400
Ten pieces. Half now.

00:30:02.480 --> 00:30:04.000
[chuckles]

00:30:02.480 --> 00:30:04.000
Six. No more.

00:30:04.080 --> 00:30:06.200
Eight and I'll

00:30:04.080 --> 00:30:06.200
make her my finest.

00:30:06.280 --> 00:30:09.280
Eight, and if she is not your

00:30:06.280 --> 00:30:09.280
finest, you will be her first.

00:30:09.360 --> 00:30:10.680
[grunts]

00:30:15.480 --> 00:30:19.920
I want this stone

00:30:15.480 --> 00:30:19.920
set into the handle?

00:30:23.960 --> 00:30:25.920
That can be done.

00:30:26.760 --> 00:30:28.840
Don't sell it nor lose it.

00:30:46.040 --> 00:30:47.760
Ale, my Lord?

00:30:47.840 --> 00:30:49.440
You stand too close, girl.

00:30:49.520 --> 00:30:52.520
Just a little to take away

00:30:49.520 --> 00:30:52.520
the taste of the gruel.

00:30:52.600 --> 00:30:54.360
You stand too close.

00:30:54.440 --> 00:30:57.240
It is broth, not gruel.

00:30:57.320 --> 00:31:01.160
-Is it?

00:30:57.320 --> 00:31:01.160
-Well, I think it is.

00:31:01.240 --> 00:31:03.160
You should be thanking God

00:31:01.240 --> 00:31:03.160
for its goodness

00:31:03.240 --> 00:31:05.680
and the banishment

00:31:03.240 --> 00:31:05.680
of those awful cramps.

00:31:05.760 --> 00:31:08.000
I am happy to eat as you eat.

00:31:08.080 --> 00:31:09.440
You are saintly, my dear.

00:31:09.520 --> 00:31:13.000
Father Beocca, join us for

00:31:09.520 --> 00:31:13.000
breakfast, I dare you.

00:31:13.080 --> 00:31:15.120
Alas, my Lord,

00:31:13.080 --> 00:31:15.120
I've already eaten.

00:31:15.200 --> 00:31:16.680
You're fortunate.

00:31:16.760 --> 00:31:20.200
Bad news, Lord.

00:31:16.760 --> 00:31:20.200
Your nephew. Aethelwold.

00:31:20.280 --> 00:31:21.600
Isn't it always?

00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:23.800
He's drunk, he's sleeping

00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:23.800
in the palace garden.

00:31:23.880 --> 00:31:27.400
Should I take him to the king?

00:31:23.880 --> 00:31:27.400
It's the second time this week.

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:30.840
May God strike him down...

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:30.840
painfully.

00:31:31.600 --> 00:31:34.320
[snoring]

00:31:36.840 --> 00:31:38.480
[grunts]

00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:40.880
-What? What?

00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:40.880
-On your feet, boy.

00:31:40.960 --> 00:31:42.160
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:31:42.240 --> 00:31:45.280
Come on,

00:31:42.240 --> 00:31:45.280
the king wants to see you.

00:31:45.360 --> 00:31:47.640
Drunk!

00:31:47.720 --> 00:31:49.120
What again?

00:31:49.200 --> 00:31:51.360
Do you think this is fit?

00:31:51.440 --> 00:31:53.560
Out, all of you, leave us.

00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:59.120
-Do you think this is fit?

00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:59.120
-I have been mistreated.

00:31:59.200 --> 00:32:01.240
I... you...

00:31:59.200 --> 00:32:01.240
you saw for yourself.

00:32:01.320 --> 00:32:05.240
I demand that this...

00:32:01.320 --> 00:32:05.240
this bear is punished.

00:32:05.320 --> 00:32:08.720
Aethelwold, your years do not hide the

00:32:05.320 --> 00:32:08.720
fact that you are a disappointment.

00:32:08.800 --> 00:32:10.960
-May I ask why?

00:32:08.800 --> 00:32:10.960
-That you need to ask

00:32:11.040 --> 00:32:13.680
tells your father

00:32:11.040 --> 00:32:13.680
all that he needs to know.

00:32:14.200 --> 00:32:15.200
What?

00:32:15.280 --> 00:32:18.560
That you are an unsuitable heir.

00:32:15.280 --> 00:32:18.560
That is what.

00:32:21.120 --> 00:32:23.280
Then I will change.

00:32:23.360 --> 00:32:25.320
-You should.

00:32:23.360 --> 00:32:25.320
-I will.

00:32:25.400 --> 00:32:29.800
All I ask is that you

00:32:25.400 --> 00:32:29.800
become a man and quickly.

00:32:29.880 --> 00:32:35.280
Today... Today, I promise.

00:32:40.520 --> 00:32:43.200
Am I excused?

00:32:49.240 --> 00:32:51.360
[mutters indistinct]

00:32:54.920 --> 00:32:58.400
I'm not convinced

00:32:54.920 --> 00:32:58.400
he is my son.

00:32:58.480 --> 00:33:00.280
If his mother was not

00:32:58.480 --> 00:33:00.280
already dead

00:33:00.360 --> 00:33:02.680
I would have her

00:33:00.360 --> 00:33:02.680
beheaded for adultery.

00:33:02.760 --> 00:33:05.920
[chuckles]

00:33:08.120 --> 00:33:11.440
If I'm to fall

00:33:08.120 --> 00:33:11.440
in the battles that will come,

00:33:11.520 --> 00:33:14.920
he cannot be king.

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:17.520
-You favor Alfred?

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:17.520
-I do.

00:33:17.600 --> 00:33:22.880
Even though

00:33:17.600 --> 00:33:22.880
he is often weak in body?

00:33:22.960 --> 00:33:25.560
Well, that his illness does

00:33:22.960 --> 00:33:25.560
not tie him to his bed,

00:33:25.640 --> 00:33:27.280
that shows the strength

00:33:25.640 --> 00:33:27.280
of my brother.

00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:31.280
Alfred is my heir, he knows it.

00:33:32.000 --> 00:33:33.920
And when the time comes,

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:40.000
Odda, my friend, you must steer

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:40.000
the Witan to make this choice.

00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:42.680
My Lord...

00:33:46.920 --> 00:33:48.280
[thunder rumbles]

00:33:48.360 --> 00:33:50.720
It's done.

00:33:50.800 --> 00:33:52.280
Should be safe for now.

00:33:52.360 --> 00:33:55.520
They say Danes

00:33:52.360 --> 00:33:55.520
rarely come here.

00:33:55.600 --> 00:33:59.760
What did Storri say to you, to

00:33:55.600 --> 00:33:59.760
make you bind his mouth and...?

00:33:59.840 --> 00:34:03.000
-He threw a curse.

00:33:59.840 --> 00:34:03.000
-Saying what?

00:34:03.080 --> 00:34:04.960
It's not important.

00:34:05.040 --> 00:34:07.160
I responded with the branch.

00:34:11.760 --> 00:34:14.680
-What are you doing?

00:34:11.760 --> 00:34:14.680
-You know what I'm doing.

00:34:14.760 --> 00:34:17.640
I'm removing the last

00:34:14.760 --> 00:34:17.640
of his curse with a kiss.

00:34:17.720 --> 00:34:19.720
I don't want to.

00:34:24.560 --> 00:34:28.600
If you want to go to the Danes

00:34:24.560 --> 00:34:28.600
then go find a new lord.

00:34:31.440 --> 00:34:33.240
It's me they wish to kill.

00:34:33.320 --> 00:34:36.800
-You sound like a child.

00:34:33.320 --> 00:34:36.800
-I'm offering you a choice.

00:34:36.880 --> 00:34:38.040
You're talking

00:34:36.880 --> 00:34:38.040
through your arse.

00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:39.640
I'm sitting on my arse.

00:34:39.720 --> 00:34:41.240
So your arse

00:34:39.720 --> 00:34:41.240
is cleverer than you,

00:34:41.320 --> 00:34:43.640
-it can do two things at once.

00:34:41.320 --> 00:34:43.640
-Thank you.

00:34:43.720 --> 00:34:44.720
[thunder rumbles]

00:34:44.800 --> 00:34:47.280
Your tongue is sharp, woman.

00:34:47.360 --> 00:34:49.960
[laughing]

00:34:50.040 --> 00:34:52.840
-Show me again.

00:34:50.040 --> 00:34:52.840
-No...

00:34:54.160 --> 00:34:56.000
You're right.

00:34:57.080 --> 00:34:59.640
We can't go to young Ragnar.

00:35:02.080 --> 00:35:06.280
But we should wait for him

00:35:02.080 --> 00:35:06.280
to find us, which he will.

00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:08.720
He will want to know the truth.

00:35:11.480 --> 00:35:14.240
In the time between,

00:35:11.480 --> 00:35:14.240
we stay alive.

00:35:14.960 --> 00:35:17.920
We pass the time.

00:35:18.000 --> 00:35:20.120
Doing what?

00:35:23.480 --> 00:35:25.200
Mm.

00:35:26.320 --> 00:35:29.040
[groans]

00:35:26.320 --> 00:35:29.040
[laughing]

00:35:53.680 --> 00:35:55.960
[laughing]

00:36:49.720 --> 00:36:52.880
I have given her some beauty

00:36:49.720 --> 00:36:52.880
but she is a tool,

00:36:52.960 --> 00:36:55.000
no more no less.

00:37:05.200 --> 00:37:08.280
She is exactly as I'd hoped.

00:37:08.360 --> 00:37:09.720
We said ten?

00:37:09.800 --> 00:37:10.760
We said eight.

00:37:10.840 --> 00:37:12.600
She's worth ten.

00:37:13.880 --> 00:37:16.400
-Thank you.

00:37:13.880 --> 00:37:16.400
-Thank you.

00:37:16.480 --> 00:37:21.640
Lord, Men have been asking

00:37:16.480 --> 00:37:21.640
of you... and your woman.

00:37:21.720 --> 00:37:24.400
-Danes or Saxon?

00:37:21.720 --> 00:37:24.400
-Take your pick.

00:37:24.480 --> 00:37:26.840
Five or more.

00:37:28.680 --> 00:37:30.720
Make her sing.

00:37:31.920 --> 00:37:34.880
[indistinct chatter]

00:37:34.960 --> 00:37:37.520
Brida, we should leave.

00:37:34.960 --> 00:37:37.520
There are men looking for us.

00:37:37.600 --> 00:37:39.040
-From Ubba?

00:37:37.600 --> 00:37:39.040
-I don't know.

00:37:39.120 --> 00:37:41.120
Saxons and Danes

00:37:39.120 --> 00:37:41.120
are looking for us

00:37:41.200 --> 00:37:43.960
we seem to be

00:37:41.200 --> 00:37:43.960
collecting enemies as we go.

00:37:50.760 --> 00:37:53.840
Get to the horses!

00:37:50.760 --> 00:37:53.840
Go! Go! Go!

00:38:07.200 --> 00:38:09.760
-Out the way! Out the way!

00:38:07.200 --> 00:38:09.760
-Hey!

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:18.080
[screams]

00:38:24.360 --> 00:38:26.720
[grunting]

00:38:47.400 --> 00:38:49.840
[bleating]

00:38:59.960 --> 00:39:01.080
[groans]

00:39:01.160 --> 00:39:03.840
[yelling]

00:39:01.160 --> 00:39:03.840
[grunting]

00:39:14.840 --> 00:39:17.240
Brida,

00:39:14.840 --> 00:39:17.240
the horses are just there.

00:39:17.320 --> 00:39:19.920
Wait there is another.

00:39:17.320 --> 00:39:19.920
We have to go. Come.

00:39:24.480 --> 00:39:27.000
[yelling]

00:39:32.280 --> 00:39:34.320
Brida, the door.

00:39:35.760 --> 00:39:37.360
Wait...

00:39:39.320 --> 00:39:40.440
Wait...

00:39:40.520 --> 00:39:43.400
Wait... now!

00:39:50.240 --> 00:39:53.000
[panting]

00:39:53.880 --> 00:39:58.080
You are right, we should leave.

00:39:58.160 --> 00:40:00.560
Whoever it was that sent them,

00:39:58.160 --> 00:40:00.560
Ubba or your uncle,

00:40:00.640 --> 00:40:04.280
they won't rest,

00:40:00.640 --> 00:40:04.280
they'll be others.

00:40:07.680 --> 00:40:10.640
I can't go home without help.

00:40:10.720 --> 00:40:14.440
Uhtred,

00:40:10.720 --> 00:40:14.440
you should forget Bebbanburg.

00:40:16.760 --> 00:40:20.440
No. No, I won't vanish.

00:40:21.600 --> 00:40:23.720
Nothing changes.

00:40:23.800 --> 00:40:26.320
Kjartan and my uncle

00:40:23.800 --> 00:40:26.320
will pay for Ragnar's death,

00:40:26.400 --> 00:40:27.960
and I will have those lands.

00:40:28.040 --> 00:40:31.080
How? With who's help?

00:40:31.160 --> 00:40:35.120
-You said yourself, we only have Ubba--

00:40:31.160 --> 00:40:35.120
-The English.

00:40:36.280 --> 00:40:38.160
If we're dead to the Danes,

00:40:36.280 --> 00:40:38.160
we have no choice.

00:40:38.240 --> 00:40:41.080
There is no England!

00:40:38.240 --> 00:40:41.080
The Danes have England.

00:40:41.160 --> 00:40:45.080
No, there is one place,

00:40:41.160 --> 00:40:45.080
south of here: it's Wessex.

00:40:45.160 --> 00:40:46.920
They'll take one look at you

00:40:45.160 --> 00:40:46.920
and kill you as a Dane.

00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:49.080
Where as Ubba will kill me

00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:49.080
as an Englishman.

00:40:49.160 --> 00:40:52.640
With King Aethelred we have

00:40:49.160 --> 00:40:52.640
a chance of everything.

00:40:53.760 --> 00:40:55.800
What do you say?

00:40:56.520 --> 00:40:58.280
Come with me.

00:41:11.320 --> 00:41:13.680
[indistinct chatter]

00:41:28.200 --> 00:41:30.760
Why do they stare?

00:41:30.840 --> 00:41:32.280
They think you're pretty.

00:41:32.680 --> 00:41:33.920
Huh!

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:39.040
Or they've never seen a Dane

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:39.040
so close, but they will.

00:42:08.840 --> 00:42:11.280
[crowd booing]

00:42:21.720 --> 00:42:23.680
We have business with the king.

00:42:21.720 --> 00:42:23.680
Aethelred.

00:42:24.160 --> 00:42:25.400
[man] Go home!

00:42:25.960 --> 00:42:28.560
[Uhtred] I say we have

00:42:25.960 --> 00:42:28.560
business with the king.

00:42:29.680 --> 00:42:31.480
Do you not understand English?

00:42:31.560 --> 00:42:35.880
Is that what you're speaking,

00:42:31.560 --> 00:42:35.880
arseling? You sound like a Dane.

00:42:35.960 --> 00:42:39.200
Why do you dress as a warrior

00:42:35.960 --> 00:42:39.200
when you're clearly a farmer?

00:42:40.920 --> 00:42:45.880
Farmer am I? I'd wager this

00:42:40.920 --> 00:42:45.880
farmer against you at anytime.

00:42:45.960 --> 00:42:47.840
We are here to see the king,

00:42:45.960 --> 00:42:47.840
peaceably.

00:42:47.920 --> 00:42:49.280
Uhtred, what are you doing?

00:42:49.360 --> 00:42:51.680
What is it farmer:

00:42:49.360 --> 00:42:51.680
first blood, or to the death?

00:42:51.760 --> 00:42:53.200
Uhtred!

00:42:53.280 --> 00:42:57.280
I'll be splitting your skull

00:42:53.280 --> 00:42:57.280
boy, so one follows the other.

00:42:57.360 --> 00:43:00.160
[crowd shouting indistinct]

00:43:00.760 --> 00:43:02.200
Uhtred?

00:43:05.400 --> 00:43:07.160
Father Beocca.

00:43:07.240 --> 00:43:08.760
[laughing]

00:43:08.840 --> 00:43:11.400
-Oh, my goodness.

00:43:08.840 --> 00:43:11.400
-You know this arseling, Father?

00:43:11.480 --> 00:43:13.360
I do. Yes, I do.

00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:17.080
Uhtred, you're...

00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:17.080
you're fully grown.

00:43:18.320 --> 00:43:19.960
And you're old!

00:43:20.040 --> 00:43:21.280
[laughing]

00:43:21.360 --> 00:43:23.240
I am.

00:43:23.320 --> 00:43:24.920
Oh, you're a man.

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:26.720
[Leofric] He claims

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:26.720
business with the king.

00:43:26.800 --> 00:43:28.840
Yes. Yes, that's true.

00:43:28.920 --> 00:43:30.680
But not with the king,

00:43:28.920 --> 00:43:30.680
it must be with Alfred.

00:43:30.760 --> 00:43:32.440
-You vouch for him?

00:43:30.760 --> 00:43:32.440
-I vouch for him.

00:43:32.520 --> 00:43:34.400
Yes, I will vouch for him.

00:43:34.480 --> 00:43:36.400
God has sent you, surely.

00:43:36.480 --> 00:43:38.480
You're a man.

00:43:39.680 --> 00:43:44.520
Father, this is Brida,

00:43:39.680 --> 00:43:44.520
my greatest friend.

00:43:44.600 --> 00:43:48.120
-A woman...

00:43:44.600 --> 00:43:48.120
-Yes.

00:43:48.520 --> 00:43:50.200
I am.

00:43:52.760 --> 00:43:54.360
I have tits.

00:43:54.920 --> 00:43:57.880
I see.

00:43:57.960 --> 00:44:00.600
Have their horses

00:43:57.960 --> 00:44:00.600
fed and watered.

00:44:00.680 --> 00:44:02.560
And I will inform Alfred

00:44:00.680 --> 00:44:02.560
that you're here with me, both.

00:44:02.640 --> 00:44:04.240
We need their weapons, Father.

00:44:04.320 --> 00:44:07.680
-Why not inform the king?

00:44:04.320 --> 00:44:07.680
-The king is busy.

00:44:07.760 --> 00:44:11.560
But you will like Alfred,

00:44:07.760 --> 00:44:11.560
he is an impressive man.

00:44:12.840 --> 00:44:14.320
Come.

00:44:16.160 --> 00:44:18.160
[bell tolls]

00:44:21.480 --> 00:44:23.240
Do you like it?

00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:25.800
I do.

00:44:27.120 --> 00:44:29.920
It's beautiful.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:32.240
You could rest here,

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:32.240
it's so quiet.

00:44:32.320 --> 00:44:34.400
[Alfred]

00:44:32.320 --> 00:44:34.400
Peaceful.

00:44:34.480 --> 00:44:37.000
The... the Romans,

00:44:34.480 --> 00:44:37.000
they built this courtyard

00:44:37.080 --> 00:44:39.920
for just that purpose,

00:44:37.080 --> 00:44:39.920
tranquility.

00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:41.400
You're Alfred?

00:44:42.120 --> 00:44:43.600
I am.

00:44:44.520 --> 00:44:46.000
My Lord.

00:44:46.080 --> 00:44:49.840
You are Uhtred. I hear word

00:44:46.080 --> 00:44:49.840
you are a considerable warrior.

00:44:49.920 --> 00:44:55.720
[chuckles] Not been tested, Lord,

00:44:49.920 --> 00:44:55.720
not yet, and I've been lucky.

00:44:55.800 --> 00:45:00.680
Well, luck is good.

00:44:55.800 --> 00:45:00.680
Or so my own warriors say.

00:45:00.760 --> 00:45:05.160
Now I haven't quite worked out

00:45:00.760 --> 00:45:05.160
the theology of luck:

00:45:05.240 --> 00:45:08.800
can there be luck

00:45:05.240 --> 00:45:08.800
if God disposes?

00:45:10.120 --> 00:45:13.240
If your God is with you,

00:45:10.120 --> 00:45:13.240
you're a lucky man.

00:45:14.760 --> 00:45:17.520
Yes. You're right.

00:45:17.600 --> 00:45:20.080
Simply put but you are right.

00:45:20.160 --> 00:45:23.200
With me,

00:45:20.160 --> 00:45:23.200
we shall talk inside, briefly.

00:45:36.640 --> 00:45:40.000
I spend

00:45:36.640 --> 00:45:40.000
much of my time in here.

00:45:40.080 --> 00:45:42.080
Do you read, Uhtred?

00:45:42.160 --> 00:45:44.520
I was schooled as a child

00:45:42.160 --> 00:45:44.520
by Father Beocca,

00:45:44.600 --> 00:45:46.320
but I was not a good student.

00:45:46.400 --> 00:45:48.440
There's much to know

00:45:46.400 --> 00:45:48.440
outside of letters.

00:45:48.520 --> 00:45:50.680
Oh, I am certain there is,

00:45:50.760 --> 00:45:54.120
but do not underestimate

00:45:50.760 --> 00:45:54.120
the power of the written word.

00:45:54.200 --> 00:45:57.440
When a man dies, if nothing is

00:45:54.200 --> 00:45:57.440
written, he is soon forgotten.

00:45:57.520 --> 00:46:00.120
For instance,

00:45:57.520 --> 00:46:00.120
who is remembering Earl Ragnar?

00:46:00.200 --> 00:46:02.760
You know of Ragnar?

00:46:02.840 --> 00:46:06.160
Father Beocca has talked

00:46:02.840 --> 00:46:06.160
much about you, Uhtred.

00:46:06.240 --> 00:46:10.480
He believed you a prisoner,

00:46:06.240 --> 00:46:10.480
a slave to Earl Ragnar.

00:46:10.560 --> 00:46:13.480
-Is that the case?

00:46:10.560 --> 00:46:13.480
-Ragnar was a father to me.

00:46:14.640 --> 00:46:16.680
I loved him.

00:46:16.760 --> 00:46:20.280
Yet, in Eoferwic, they are

00:46:16.760 --> 00:46:20.280
saying that you killed him.

00:46:20.360 --> 00:46:22.120
They lie.

00:46:24.800 --> 00:46:28.160
Karjartan, Karjartan,

00:46:24.800 --> 00:46:28.160
is that how you pronounce it?

00:46:28.240 --> 00:46:29.160
Kjartan?

00:46:29.240 --> 00:46:30.480
Kjartan...

00:46:30.560 --> 00:46:33.360
...has benefited most

00:46:30.560 --> 00:46:33.360
from Ragnar's death,

00:46:33.440 --> 00:46:36.400
he has taken his place

00:46:33.440 --> 00:46:36.400
and is Earl Kjartan now.

00:46:36.480 --> 00:46:37.920
A great lord, with ships.

00:46:38.000 --> 00:46:39.480
That's written down?

00:46:39.560 --> 00:46:43.640
Whatever I discover about

00:46:39.560 --> 00:46:43.640
my enemies is written down.

00:46:43.720 --> 00:46:46.480
It is in Kjartan's interest

00:46:43.720 --> 00:46:46.480
to kill you, is it not?

00:46:46.560 --> 00:46:49.960
He would not want Ragnar's son

00:46:46.560 --> 00:46:49.960
to hear a different tale.

00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:52.680
He would not wish him

00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:52.680
to hear the truth, no.

00:46:52.760 --> 00:46:55.680
No... And the Chieftain Ubba...

00:46:55.760 --> 00:46:58.120
Although he himself

00:46:55.760 --> 00:46:58.120
has now traveled north,

00:46:58.200 --> 00:47:01.800
he has sent men to Mercia,

00:46:58.200 --> 00:47:01.800
asking of your whereabouts,

00:47:01.880 --> 00:47:05.240
but not your welfare I surmise?

00:47:05.320 --> 00:47:06.920
How do you come by all of this?

00:47:07.000 --> 00:47:10.480
I have eyes and ears

00:47:07.000 --> 00:47:10.480
in each of the kingdoms.

00:47:14.320 --> 00:47:17.360
One day, it is my hope

00:47:17.440 --> 00:47:23.760
that all kingdoms will become

00:47:17.440 --> 00:47:23.760
one united under one God.

00:47:24.280 --> 00:47:26.000
One king?

00:47:27.080 --> 00:47:31.160
If all men can agree, yes.

00:47:31.240 --> 00:47:36.480
All that remains of England,

00:47:31.240 --> 00:47:36.480
is Wessex.

00:47:36.560 --> 00:47:40.880
The birth of an England,

00:47:36.560 --> 00:47:40.880
the idea...

00:47:40.960 --> 00:47:46.320
of a single kingdom...

00:47:40.960 --> 00:47:46.320
called England

00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:48.720
has to begin here.

00:47:49.840 --> 00:47:51.560
There is nowhere else.

00:47:51.640 --> 00:47:53.600
But for how long

00:47:51.640 --> 00:47:53.600
will Wessex remain?

00:47:54.760 --> 00:47:58.840
The fate of Wessex will be determined

00:47:54.760 --> 00:47:58.840
by Englishmen, all Englishmen.

00:47:59.480 --> 00:48:04.000
Only by joining together and

00:47:59.480 --> 00:48:04.000
saving Wessex can we have England.

00:48:05.040 --> 00:48:07.680
Only by saving Wessex

00:48:05.040 --> 00:48:07.680
can we have a...

00:48:08.280 --> 00:48:12.560
...a Northumbria,

00:48:08.280 --> 00:48:12.560
a Bebbanburg.

00:48:12.640 --> 00:48:14.680
And if Wessex

00:48:12.640 --> 00:48:14.680
can't be saved?

00:48:15.040 --> 00:48:17.840
Then we are all no more.

00:48:18.520 --> 00:48:20.120
[bell tolls]

00:48:21.640 --> 00:48:23.080
Prayers.

00:48:28.040 --> 00:48:29.880
[breathes heavily]

00:48:29.960 --> 00:48:32.160
And a little discomfort...

00:48:37.600 --> 00:48:39.440
I will summarize.

00:48:40.040 --> 00:48:42.760
The Danes

00:48:40.040 --> 00:48:42.760
are gathering a great army,

00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:44.520
they have, in fact,

00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:44.520
gathered an army.

00:48:44.880 --> 00:48:45.880
They gather where?

00:48:45.960 --> 00:48:48.040
They have moved up river

00:48:45.960 --> 00:48:48.040
from Lundene to Readingum.

00:48:48.120 --> 00:48:50.200
They are settling as we speak.

00:48:50.280 --> 00:48:52.080
But you say Ubba is in the

00:48:50.280 --> 00:48:52.080
north, so who leads them?

00:48:52.160 --> 00:48:56.720
-The Earl Guthrum leads them.

00:48:52.160 --> 00:48:56.720
-I know Guthrum.

00:48:56.800 --> 00:49:02.960
We will need every advantage

00:48:56.800 --> 00:49:02.960
and Father Beocca considers you,

00:49:03.040 --> 00:49:06.240
Uhtred of Bebbanburg,

00:49:03.040 --> 00:49:06.240
to be an advantage,

00:49:06.320 --> 00:49:09.760
whereas I believe

00:49:06.320 --> 00:49:09.760
you are here solely to hide,

00:49:09.840 --> 00:49:11.720
to save yourself.

00:49:14.680 --> 00:49:19.000
I look at you and I see a Dane.

00:49:19.080 --> 00:49:24.160
I see Uhtred of Nowhere, who

00:49:19.080 --> 00:49:24.160
cares for no one, but himself.

00:49:26.200 --> 00:49:29.680
Now, I must go to prayers.

00:49:26.200 --> 00:49:29.680
You will join me?

00:49:29.760 --> 00:49:31.200
[chuckles]

00:49:31.280 --> 00:49:35.760
-If my Lord will excuse me?

00:49:31.280 --> 00:49:35.760
-[Brida] Us both.

00:49:35.840 --> 00:49:40.720
Of course. I expected as much.

00:49:40.800 --> 00:49:43.160
-Father Beocca!

00:49:40.800 --> 00:49:43.160
-Lord...

00:49:43.240 --> 00:49:46.240
-Take your guests for refreshments.

00:49:43.240 --> 00:49:46.240
-I will my Lord.

00:49:46.320 --> 00:49:49.720
They may remain in Winchester,

00:49:46.320 --> 00:49:49.720
but I hold you responsible.

00:49:49.800 --> 00:49:51.640
Yes, Lord.

00:49:56.320 --> 00:49:59.360
You should have gone along and prayed

00:49:56.320 --> 00:49:59.360
with him, it would have bonded you.

00:49:59.440 --> 00:50:00.920
He believes we are Pagans.

00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:03.640
What Alfred believes is that

00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:03.640
the Danes have abandoned you.

00:50:03.720 --> 00:50:06.720
Ubba has abandoned us

00:50:03.720 --> 00:50:06.720
there are other lords.

00:50:06.800 --> 00:50:09.000
Most, if not all, follow Ubba.

00:50:09.080 --> 00:50:11.320
So believe me girl,

00:50:09.080 --> 00:50:11.320
you have been abandoned!

00:50:11.400 --> 00:50:13.040
Yeah, you know everything

00:50:11.400 --> 00:50:13.040
about the Danes don't you?

00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:15.840
This way,

00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:15.840
I want to show you something.

00:50:18.440 --> 00:50:20.440
The Charters of Bebbanburg.

00:50:20.520 --> 00:50:24.560
-Yeah, the land books, yeah.

00:50:20.520 --> 00:50:24.560
-You kept them safe.

00:50:24.640 --> 00:50:26.720
I have shown

00:50:24.640 --> 00:50:26.720
them to Alfred he...

00:50:26.800 --> 00:50:30.320
...he knows that you are

00:50:26.800 --> 00:50:30.320
the Ealdorman by right.

00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:36.520
I will continue to keep them

00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:36.520
safe, but Uhtred, you...

00:50:36.600 --> 00:50:38.760
You must behave

00:50:36.600 --> 00:50:38.760
like an Ealdorman.

00:50:48.520 --> 00:50:50.320
The charters have no meaning,

00:50:50.400 --> 00:50:51.920
Northumbria belongs

00:50:50.400 --> 00:50:51.920
to the Danes.

00:50:52.000 --> 00:50:53.400
[Beocca]

00:50:52.000 --> 00:50:53.400
It does not belong to the Danes,

00:50:53.480 --> 00:50:54.720
it has been stolen by them.

00:50:54.800 --> 00:50:56.640
[Brida]

00:50:54.800 --> 00:50:56.640
If you want wealth, you take it!

00:50:56.720 --> 00:50:58.120
You can't ignore what's true.

00:50:58.200 --> 00:51:00.120
If the Danes are at Readingum,

00:50:58.200 --> 00:51:00.120
I will go to Readingum.

00:51:00.200 --> 00:51:02.400
-What?

00:51:00.200 --> 00:51:02.400
-For what purpose?

00:51:02.480 --> 00:51:03.880
For knowledge.

00:51:03.960 --> 00:51:06.200
We have knowledge and you should

00:51:03.960 --> 00:51:06.200
stay away from Danes.

00:51:06.280 --> 00:51:07.720
For new knowledge.

00:51:07.800 --> 00:51:10.440
You know where they're settling

00:51:07.800 --> 00:51:10.440
but you don't know why.

00:51:10.520 --> 00:51:12.400
[Beocca] We know their number

00:51:10.520 --> 00:51:12.400
and their position.

00:51:12.480 --> 00:51:15.960
Not their intention.

00:51:12.480 --> 00:51:15.960
Am I a prisoner?

00:51:16.800 --> 00:51:19.280
Their intention is to attack.

00:51:19.800 --> 00:51:21.920
When?

00:51:22.000 --> 00:51:23.480
Spring. It's always spring.

00:51:23.560 --> 00:51:25.960
I'll go to Readingum

00:51:23.560 --> 00:51:25.960
Where is it?

00:51:26.040 --> 00:51:27.960
-It's too dangerous.

00:51:26.040 --> 00:51:27.960
-Not for me.

00:51:28.040 --> 00:51:31.320
-I'm a godless stain remember!

00:51:28.040 --> 00:51:31.320
-So why spy for Alfred?

00:51:31.400 --> 00:51:34.000
Because he is

00:51:31.400 --> 00:51:34.000
an Ealdorman of England.

00:51:38.640 --> 00:51:40.960
[indistinct chatter]

00:51:41.680 --> 00:51:42.960
[door opens]

00:51:44.160 --> 00:51:45.800
[Beocca]

00:51:44.160 --> 00:51:45.800
Lord.

00:51:45.880 --> 00:51:49.240
Regarding the conversion

00:51:45.880 --> 00:51:49.240
of the Pagans to Christianity?

00:51:49.320 --> 00:51:50.360
Yes, Lord?

00:51:50.440 --> 00:51:52.400
How do we decide what is proper?

00:51:52.480 --> 00:51:56.240
To enlighten them

00:51:52.480 --> 00:51:56.240
or to kill them?

00:51:56.320 --> 00:51:59.640
Spreading God's word

00:51:56.320 --> 00:51:59.640
is of course our mission,

00:51:59.720 --> 00:52:03.320
but I fear that the Pagans,

00:51:59.720 --> 00:52:03.320
the true Pagans,

00:52:03.400 --> 00:52:07.280
must first witness,

00:52:03.400 --> 00:52:07.280
then feel his power.

00:52:14.560 --> 00:52:17.960
-Uhtred... will return?

00:52:14.560 --> 00:52:17.960
-Yes, he will return.

00:52:18.040 --> 00:52:20.440
Yes, but how will he return?

00:52:18.040 --> 00:52:20.440
As who? As what?

00:52:20.520 --> 00:52:24.640
-I know this boy--

00:52:20.520 --> 00:52:24.640
-This boy is now a man.

00:52:24.720 --> 00:52:27.680
-I know his soul.

00:52:24.720 --> 00:52:27.680
-Father Beocca, he has no soul.

00:52:27.760 --> 00:52:33.240
And you say yourself, the Pagans

00:52:27.760 --> 00:52:33.240
need to feel the power of God.

00:52:33.320 --> 00:52:35.680
It is written now, here.

00:52:35.760 --> 00:52:39.000
You may leave me.

00:52:39.080 --> 00:52:42.680
We shall see what

00:52:39.080 --> 00:52:42.680
the days bring, my Lord.

00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:07.120
If resting through the winter

00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:07.120
was their intention,

00:53:07.200 --> 00:53:09.600
they would have

00:53:07.200 --> 00:53:09.600
remained in Lundene. Yes?

00:53:10.680 --> 00:53:12.360
It's you who is Alfred's spy.

00:53:12.440 --> 00:53:14.680
The next step is to kill

00:53:12.440 --> 00:53:14.680
for him. Will you do that?

00:53:14.760 --> 00:53:18.480
Answer me this... If we were to cross this

00:53:14.760 --> 00:53:18.480
river and find Guthrum, what would happen?

00:53:18.560 --> 00:53:23.040
He'd kill us both.

00:53:18.560 --> 00:53:23.040
We owe them nothing!

00:53:23.120 --> 00:53:24.880
Alfred needs to know

00:53:23.120 --> 00:53:24.880
about the Danes,

00:53:24.960 --> 00:53:26.520
and I need to win his trust!

00:53:26.600 --> 00:53:29.720
You'd think he'd deliver you

00:53:26.600 --> 00:53:29.720
Bebbanburg, what if you're wrong?

00:53:48.040 --> 00:53:51.040
Alfred, you have called council,

00:53:48.040 --> 00:53:51.040
for what reason?

00:53:51.120 --> 00:53:52.920
Lord forgive me, it may well be

00:53:51.120 --> 00:53:52.920
for no good reason,

00:53:53.000 --> 00:53:54.440
but we have a Pagan in court

00:53:54.520 --> 00:53:56.640
who claims to have knowledge

00:53:54.520 --> 00:53:56.640
regarding the Dane army.

00:53:56.720 --> 00:53:59.720
-A Pagan?

00:53:56.720 --> 00:53:59.720
-Forgive me, Lord, he is Uhtred of Bebbanburg.

00:53:59.800 --> 00:54:02.400
I vouch for his word.

00:54:02.480 --> 00:54:04.440
Uhtred.

00:54:06.280 --> 00:54:07.440
Lord...

00:54:10.560 --> 00:54:13.000
I have been to Readingum.

00:54:10.560 --> 00:54:13.000
I have watched the Danes.

00:54:13.080 --> 00:54:14.680
Their intention

00:54:13.080 --> 00:54:14.680
is not to settle.

00:54:14.760 --> 00:54:17.160
If it were, they would have

00:54:14.760 --> 00:54:17.160
remained in Lundene.

00:54:17.240 --> 00:54:19.680
You are saying what,

00:54:17.240 --> 00:54:19.680
that they intend to attack?

00:54:19.760 --> 00:54:21.280
-I am Lord.

00:54:19.760 --> 00:54:21.280
-[Odda] We already know this.

00:54:21.360 --> 00:54:22.880
Come spring,

00:54:21.360 --> 00:54:22.880
they'll be at our door.

00:54:22.960 --> 00:54:24.960
They will be marching within

00:54:22.960 --> 00:54:24.960
days, Lord, I am sure of it.

00:54:25.040 --> 00:54:26.520
How can you possibly

00:54:25.040 --> 00:54:26.520
be sure of it?

00:54:26.600 --> 00:54:28.160
The ground is sodden all

00:54:26.600 --> 00:54:28.160
around, it makes no sense.

00:54:28.240 --> 00:54:29.640
They have made their sacrifices.

00:54:28.240 --> 00:54:29.640
The ordinary warriors

00:54:29.720 --> 00:54:31.680
have caught and killed birds,

00:54:29.720 --> 00:54:31.680
jackdaws.

00:54:31.760 --> 00:54:33.920
This is only done

00:54:31.760 --> 00:54:33.920
in the days before battle.

00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:35.240
And they are hungry.

00:54:35.320 --> 00:54:37.080
Then perhaps they have

00:54:35.320 --> 00:54:37.080
eaten these jackdaws.

00:54:37.160 --> 00:54:39.440
They have many hundreds of men

00:54:37.160 --> 00:54:39.440
and horses, and few supplies.

00:54:39.520 --> 00:54:42.440
They'll first seize a town

00:54:39.520 --> 00:54:42.440
rich with grain and livestock.

00:54:42.520 --> 00:54:44.680
I don't know the country well,

00:54:42.520 --> 00:54:44.680
but I have traveled,

00:54:44.760 --> 00:54:47.600
I believe

00:54:44.760 --> 00:54:47.600
Abbendum is such a place.

00:54:47.680 --> 00:54:52.160
To defeat the Danes you must meet

00:54:47.680 --> 00:54:52.160
them on the road to Abbendum.

00:54:52.520 --> 00:54:54.680
It will be within days, Lord.

00:54:54.760 --> 00:54:56.120
You went to Readingum alone?

00:54:56.200 --> 00:54:59.240
-With Brida.

00:54:56.200 --> 00:54:59.240
-Why alone?

00:55:00.120 --> 00:55:01.200
Why not?

00:55:01.280 --> 00:55:02.280
Because for most of your life

00:55:02.360 --> 00:55:03.280
you have lived as a Dane.

00:55:03.360 --> 00:55:04.560
You look like a Dane,

00:55:04.640 --> 00:55:06.040
you can speak

00:55:04.640 --> 00:55:06.040
the language of a Dane,

00:55:06.120 --> 00:55:09.120
therefore, I surmise you can

00:55:06.120 --> 00:55:09.120
set a trap like a Dane.

00:55:09.200 --> 00:55:11.560
Agreed, my Lord,

00:55:09.200 --> 00:55:11.560
he imagines we are jackdaws.

00:55:11.640 --> 00:55:13.640
[Aethelred]

00:55:11.640 --> 00:55:13.640
Where, on the road to Abbendum?

00:55:13.720 --> 00:55:15.320
Where would you choose

00:55:13.720 --> 00:55:15.320
to meet their army?

00:55:15.400 --> 00:55:17.360
I would choose the place

00:55:15.400 --> 00:55:17.360
called Asec's Hill, Lord.

00:55:17.440 --> 00:55:19.360
You would choose

00:55:17.440 --> 00:55:19.360
or Guthrum would choose?

00:55:19.440 --> 00:55:22.160
I have seen it, the pass narrows,

00:55:19.440 --> 00:55:22.160
you cannot be out-flanked.

00:55:22.240 --> 00:55:24.720
For the Danes to fight uphill,

00:55:22.240 --> 00:55:24.720
it will be difficult,

00:55:24.800 --> 00:55:27.320
but they'll be confident,

00:55:24.800 --> 00:55:27.320
they do not fear West Saxons.

00:55:27.400 --> 00:55:29.880
Why? Why do they not fear us?

00:55:29.960 --> 00:55:33.760
They believe you to be farmers,

00:55:29.960 --> 00:55:33.760
nothing more.

00:55:33.840 --> 00:55:35.560
So even with the sun

00:55:33.840 --> 00:55:35.560
in their eyes,

00:55:35.640 --> 00:55:37.520
which is possible, they will

00:55:35.640 --> 00:55:37.520
climb the hill to fight,

00:55:37.600 --> 00:55:39.040
and that can be

00:55:37.600 --> 00:55:39.040
to our advantage.

00:55:39.120 --> 00:55:41.160
[Odda]

00:55:39.120 --> 00:55:41.160
To our advantage, he says!

00:55:41.240 --> 00:55:44.360
You have been here for a matter of days

00:55:41.240 --> 00:55:44.360
and already you claim to be of Wessex?

00:55:44.440 --> 00:55:47.880
This is nonsense, this is all

00:55:44.440 --> 00:55:47.880
far too convenient, my Lord.

00:55:47.960 --> 00:55:50.400
My Lord, my sword was made by

00:55:47.960 --> 00:55:50.400
a Saxon smith.

00:55:50.480 --> 00:55:51.800
My sword is for Wessex.

00:55:51.880 --> 00:55:53.120
Do not interrupt a noble

00:55:51.880 --> 00:55:53.120
when he is speaking!

00:55:53.200 --> 00:55:55.120
-[Aethelred] Odda.

00:55:53.200 --> 00:55:55.120
-I believe this man,

00:55:55.200 --> 00:55:57.040
and this bag of rags that

00:55:55.200 --> 00:55:57.040
follows him, to be imposters.

00:55:57.120 --> 00:55:59.560
No army marches

00:55:57.120 --> 00:55:59.560
as winter approaches, never.

00:55:59.640 --> 00:56:01.400
Young Odda,

00:55:59.640 --> 00:56:01.400
enough from you now!

00:56:02.520 --> 00:56:04.040
My Lord.

00:56:08.480 --> 00:56:11.280
You...

00:56:11.360 --> 00:56:14.760
You have spoken and given

00:56:11.360 --> 00:56:14.760
this council much to discuss.

00:56:14.840 --> 00:56:16.360
My Lord.

00:56:18.760 --> 00:56:22.800
Alfred, he's here at your

00:56:18.760 --> 00:56:22.800
invitation. What now?

00:56:22.880 --> 00:56:27.120
Should the Danes march,

00:56:22.880 --> 00:56:27.120
we must face them.

00:56:27.200 --> 00:56:28.680
And I would rather be

00:56:28.760 --> 00:56:31.720
at the top of a hill

00:56:28.760 --> 00:56:31.720
than on the flat.

00:56:31.800 --> 00:56:34.960
I say we march to Asec's Hill.

00:56:36.240 --> 00:56:41.360
But... take him.

00:56:41.440 --> 00:56:43.120
Take them both

00:56:41.440 --> 00:56:43.120
and make them secure.

00:56:43.200 --> 00:56:45.200
My Lord? What is this?

00:56:45.280 --> 00:56:47.000
I have spoken the truth!

00:56:47.080 --> 00:56:50.480
-I have spoken the truth! Father Beocca!

00:56:47.080 --> 00:56:50.480
-My Lord, please.

00:56:50.560 --> 00:56:55.400
-Beocca, help me! Beocca!

00:56:50.560 --> 00:56:55.400
-Have faith!

00:56:55.480 --> 00:56:58.280
[grunting]

00:57:24.000 --> 00:57:26.680
[man speaks foreign language]

00:57:39.560 --> 00:57:41.040
Halt!

00:57:47.480 --> 00:57:49.440
[man] Left flank, hold!

00:57:49.520 --> 00:57:51.720
Hold!

00:57:51.800 --> 00:57:54.120
Archers ready!

00:58:01.560 --> 00:58:03.320
On my command.

00:58:03.400 --> 00:58:08.160
For God. For Wessex.

00:58:03.400 --> 00:58:08.160
For England!

00:58:08.240 --> 00:58:11.080
[men cheering]